                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's unfortunate that a Rythm game gets a bad review from me... I thought I saw a lot of potential on this game. However, once I installed it and gave it a try there was nothing on it.\nSure the game had a few good attempts at being nice with 2 of the songs I barely heard, but the main problem is from the begining. You cannot modify even the controls, even though the game shows you a so called option for it, you cannot even navigate through the main menu. You're prompted to play a game without knowing the controls, which are by default keys that are not designed to being pressed from 3 at the time (Any kind of gamer has suffered this little setback once or twice) There's no feedback on the timing of your game, no progression or choosing of your songs... There is.. Nothing...\n\nI went to the disscusion board to see if there was something, a few months ago the dev said that was give it a hand on something and there was no modification on the things I've seen.\n\nI won't even bother in refound the game as it was extremely cheap... But even that I wouldn't recommend this kind of incomplete game to anyone even if the game was free.",
